iIDfynfW-ka_j-mIfNpEMrvWrifY" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Big Website=E2=80=
=99s Ultimate 1-50</a>, a rundown of the male footballers best associated w=
ith each squad number. It=E2=80=99s lighthearted reading designed to entert=
ain, maybe even inform, and perhaps spark a few memories and a touch of deb=
ate. Or, if you prefer, a rage-bait waste of time that shames the internet.=
 Where the hell is Roy Keane! How dare you leave out Bobby Moore! And Pel=
=C3=A9? A list without Pel=C3=A9? I don=E2=80=99t want to live in a world w=
here there are lists without Pel=C3=A9.<br><br>Such is the world these days=
, though surely a certain amount of respect is due to an exercise that shun=
s Lionel Messi and Zinedine Zidane but can welcome in Salvatore Sirigu and =
Mateusz Klich. And true, it might be a challenging read for those (and, let=
=E2=80=99s be clear, we=E2=80=99re absolutely definitely not referring to o=
urselves here, no sirree) old enough to have been brought up in an era of 1=
; 2, 5, 6, 3; 7, 4, 8, 11; 9 (big man), 10 (little man). The days of two su=
bstitutes who wore Nos 12 and 14. The days of a quarter of wine gums in you=
r pocket and misty rain drifting across the floodlights and =E2=80=A6 oh my=
 god Asamoah Gyan is wearing No 3 and playing up front. This is not a drill=
. Repeat this is not a drill. Burn it all down, the game=E2=80=99s gone.<br=
><br>There is something about it all that does invoke strangely strong reac=
tions, but every day is a school day. So, yes, there remains a hallowed aur=
a around 1-11 but even some of the game=E2=80=99s greats =E2=80=93 we=E2=80=
=99re looking at you Gerd M=C3=BCller and Johan Cruyff =E2=80=93 are best a=
ssociated with numbers outside of the traditional undectet. And, as <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18I=
RyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgVDIHEFTu1KYuAnMfEg8lF1tv-6c9FjW=
bpOrtGS746_msieE0uuHZ-gtCwDs2pZOnBRf3g_PsbilAEGhcTlDEWIlWtcgXjU3P-JtxSfV3Oa=
jtLH6kSKm_p2H8C9xYvUOeIt7LtBMQ5dk4CTN5OQcaX8o2_qrkIvjtkUeJR4wrvwUxTdCYs3v5o=
8grjCwzSnYwrEeWb7KiTF0liSxiqDwdnm6NvuinTuUlfaeYcPwEVnc/4vm/1aA0nD04RoKsCqsl=
9KLfvA/h29/h001.-qFz2zUMLwSgAz-daWz6xCGcuiFoANIPOPFIadltXNw" style=3D"color=
: #0077B6;">Jonathan Wilson brilliantly illustrates here</a>, there=E2=80=
=99s a risk of being a bit Eurocentric when it comes to numbering =E2=80=93=
 Argentina=E2=80=99s tactical evolution, for example, meant their tradition=
al back four lines up 4, 2, 6, 3, with the No 5 in central midfield. Brazil=
 too has No 5 as the defensive midfielder, with the standard back four as 4=
, 2, 3, 6. And don=E2=80=99t get us started on Hungary at Wembley in 1953 =
=E2=80=93 Nandor Hidegkuti, you rascal! So do yourself a favour and dig int=
o today=E2=80=99s offering. You might learn something. Or you might just ge=
t really, really cross about Curtis Jones. Either way, it=E2=80=99s win-win=
.</p></div></td></tr>
